# Per-Dockerfile ignore for Dockerfile.web, which BuildKit prefers over the
# global .dockerignore when building with `file: Dockerfile.web`.
#
# The global .dockerignore excludes apps/web on purpose: the Python release
# image would otherwise pack node_modules and the vite output into a layer that
# should be 100kB. That exclusion is correct for Dockerfile.python and stays.
#
# But Dockerfile.web builds from the repository root and copies apps/web
# explicitly, so the same exclusion made its COPY steps fail with
# "/apps/web": not found. This file keeps apps/web in the context for the web
# image only, while still dropping everything that image has no use for --
# including node_modules and dist, which is what the global rule was really
# protecting against.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite

**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

.git
.venv
.env
.env.*

# The web image needs apps/web and nothing else from the tree.
src
config
scripts
oracle
migrations
tests
fixtures
examples
infra
ci
runtime
reports
data
docs
deliverables
ops
